; --- E1-11: On day 1 of Year 1, Pell collected silken threads from the lanterns of the Cliff Path at dawn. Nightmoths had landed on the lanterns during the night. The nightmoths had left silken threads on the lanterns. Pell carried the silken threads to Cauldron Hall. Hesper filled the three cauldrons with sea-water from the Salt-bloom Tide-pools. Hesper boiled the silken threads in the sea-water. Mire-essence formed in the three cauldrons by evening. Hesper stored the mire-essence in three clay vessels.
(sem-graph E1-11)
(sem-graph-kind E1-11 neo-davidsonian)
(doc-graph aelmere E1-11)
