; --- E1-12: On day 3 of Year 1, the keepers of the East Row together lit the lanterns of the East Row at sundown. The keepers of the East Row tended the lanterns that night. The lanterns burned mire-essence. Together, the lanterns produced mist-light. The lanterns showed mist-light at night. The mist-light attracted nightmoths. Many of the nightmoths gathered at the lanterns. The nightmoths landed on the lanterns. The nightmoths left silken threads on the lanterns. Pell collected the silken threads from the lanterns at dawn on day 4 of Year 1. Hesper boiled the silken threads in sea-water on day 4 of Year 1. Mire-essence formed in a cauldron by evening. Hesper stored the mire-essence in two clay vessels. The keepers of the East Row lit the lanterns of the East Row with the stored mire-essence at sundown on day 4 of Year 1.
(sem-graph E1-12)
(sem-graph-kind E1-12 neo-davidsonian)
(doc-graph aelmere E1-12)
