; --- E2-04: On day 17 of Year 1, Keepers had relit the eleven lanterns of the Middle Row. The eleven lanterns burned dimly. The dim lanterns gave weak mist-light. The weak mist-light attracted a handful of nightmoths. Keepers counted twelve nightmoths at the Middle Row that night. The thread harvest at the Middle Row fell. Pell and Coraline Ash collected a handful of silken threads from the Middle Row the next morning. Hesper boiled the silken threads in sea-water at Cauldron Hall that day. The cauldrons yielded two vessels of mire-essence. The cauldrons had yielded three vessels of mire-essence on day 1.
(sem-graph E2-04)
