; --- E4-01: On day 60 of Year 1, about four sky-cats were visible on the cliff-spires in the morning. In a normal autumn about ten sky-cats are visible on the cliff-spires in the morning. A handful of sky-cats had been visible on the cliff-spires for two weeks. A handful of sky-cats had hunted on the Cliff Path in those two weeks. A handful of sky-cats had molted in those two weeks. Tessa Brae collected about twelve feathers per morning during those two weeks. In a normal autumn Tessa Brae collects about thirty-five feathers per morning.
