; --- E7-01: On day 210 of Year 1, the spring equinox came. On day 216 of Year 1, the moon was full. The Council closed the salt-bloom season at the full-moon meeting. The Northcove resumed its usual production. The stations of the Cliff Path stepped down salt-bloom additions during the following two weeks. The thread harvests returned to spring levels. Cauldron Hall began a heavier distillation cycle. The feather store held three weeks of supply at the end of the winter. About ten sky-cats were visible on the cliff-spires in the morning by the spring equinox.
