; --- E7-09: On day 300 of Year 1, the keepers of the Harbor Row together lit the lanterns of the Harbor Row at sundown. The lanterns burned mire-essence. Together, the lanterns produced mist-light. The lanterns showed mist-light at night. The mist-light attracted nightmoths. A crowd of nightmoths gathered at the Harbor Row. Three sky-cats descended from the cliff-spires. The three sky-cats hunted the nightmoth crowd at the Harbor Row in summer. The nightmoth crowd at the Harbor Row shrank. Some nightmoths survived the hunt. The surviving nightmoths fled to the Hollows. The surviving nightmoths reached the Hollows. The three sky-cats molted during the hunt. The nightmoths left silken threads on the lanterns of the Harbor Row.
