; --- E10-02: On day 555 of Year 2, the spring equinox came. The day was clear and warm. The Council closed the salt-bloom season at the next full-moon meeting. The stations of the Cliff Path stepped down salt-bloom additions during the following two weeks. The Northcove returned to its summer cadence. Cauldron Hall increased its distillation. Hesper assigned an extra apprentice to the morning collection of silken threads.
