; --- E10-09: On day 690 of Year 2, Old Vesh asked the Council whether the sealed records in the Watch should be opened. Brindle Coombe argued that the sealed records had been sealed for a reason. Meren Tallowhand agreed with Brindle Coombe. Old Vesh said that the open records alone shaped the village's memory. The Council declined to open the sealed records. The Council tabled the matter. The Council agreed to revisit the question at the autumn-equinox meeting.
